{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgA8f4CEhZS1vRC44FfHE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `fd foo --and one/two` now gives the same \"contains a path-separation character\" error as `fd one/two`. Before, a separator in an `--and` pattern was ignored and the search just returned nothing.\n\n- **`src/main.rs`:** `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs the same check on every pattern: the primary one and each `--and`. The Windows `\\` rule (only flagged when the pattern names a real directory) applies to all of them too. `--full-path` still skips the check.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** new test `test_and_pattern_with_path_separator`. It checks that `--and one/two` fails, and that with `--full-path` the same search runs and returns results.\n\nAll tests pass, and clippy shows no new warnings in the changed code.\n\n**Not checked:** the Windows path, since I could only run on Linux. The error text suggests `fd . '<pattern>'`, which reads slightly oddly when the bad pattern came from `--and`, but it's still correct, so I left it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":38717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":161,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":341,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b969753-13b8-4e20-93db-b7e2d655cdfa","uuid":"f097baaf-aa0d-40d7-ab2a-64fb9340871a","timestamp":"2026-10-18T17:55:42.043Z","request_id":"req_011CgA8f41Kjz8iG35yQqwAt"}
